questions.rationale_md:
FM-08 shows that advisory assemblies fade, including Ireland's own. So bodies chosen by lot have **binding power where elected politicians have a conflict of interest**:

- **auditing officials' pay and privileges** (FM-01);
- **approving any extension of emergency powers** (FM-15);
- **oversight of the security services** (FM-04);
- **the right to force a referendum**.

Ordinary law-making stays with elected, recallable delegates.
